                                "sense_id": "c218b865-307a-3e38-af9c-74ae723e8753",
                                "text": "1906-1907, Mark Twain, Chapters from My Autobiography\nAutobiography […] inevitably consists mainly of extinctions of the truth, shirkings of the truth, partial revealments of the truth, with hardly an instance of plain straight truth […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dde7facd-36c3-446e-964e-f92e26cad981",
                                "sense_id": "c218b865-307a-3e38-af9c-74ae723e8753",
                                "text": "Midler has never been called a feminist, but one cannot call her anything else better. Every move in her career appears to be one more shirking of categorization."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
